The P-256 complete projective addition formulas and Ed25519 extended-coordinate
formulas and verification behavior in curves.goml are adapted from the Go 1.25
standard library sources crypto/internal/fips140/nistec/p256.go,
crypto/internal/fips140/edwards25519/edwards25519.go, and
crypto/internal/fips140/ed25519/ed25519.go. The Go license is in LICENSE-GO.

P-256 uses the complete a = -3 formulas in Appendix A.2 of Renes, Costello,
and Batina, Complete addition formulas for prime order elliptic curves (2015).
Ed25519 implements the pure Ed25519 algorithm of RFC 8032, retaining Go
crypto/ed25519 verification behavior for noncanonical public-point encodings.

Field and scalar operations use fixed eight-limb Montgomery arithmetic. Scalar
multiplication and inversion use fixed 256-round schedules and masked selection;
P-256 nonces come from std::crypto::rand. These source-level properties do not
provide a compiler-enforced or independently audited constant-time guarantee.
